Campfire for BEAM: wallet-api connects to its node through a SOCKS5 proxy (Tor), fail closed.

BEAM is a privacy chain: the user's IP address must never reach a BEAM node. Stock
wallet-api has no proxy option at all; beam-wallet does (--proxy, --proxy_addr,
wallet/cli/cli.cpp). This patch gives wallet-api the same two options and sets them
on its FlyClient::NetworkStd exactly as beam-wallet does (m_Cfg.m_UseProxy,
m_Cfg.m_ProxyAddr). core/fly_client.cpp then routes the first connection and every
reconnect through the proxy; SBBS messages travel over that same node connection.

Fail closed:
 * no direct fallback: while the proxy is unreachable the wallet is offline;
 * with --proxy=1, --node_addr must be an IPv4 literal ("a.b.c.d:port"). BEAM's SOCKS5
   client only sends IPv4 (ATYP 1), so a host name would be resolved by the system
   resolver, outside the proxy. wallet-api refuses to start instead and never calls
   the resolver for it. The app resolves host names through Tor itself (SOCKS5
   RESOLVE, 0xF0) and passes the address;
 * --proxy_addr must be an IPv4 literal as well.
wallet-api has no runtime node switch (NodeNetwork::setNodeAddress, which would
resolve names and the default peer list, is never called by wallet-api), so the node
address cannot change behind the proxy's back.

Without --proxy (the default) behaviour is unchanged. Written against tag
beam-7.5.14493 + the core series (../../patches 0001-0006, which already patch this
file in 0002); it can move into the core series as is. patch -p1.

--- a/wallet/api/cli/api_cli.cpp
+++ b/wallet/api/cli/api_cli.cpp
@@ -74,6 +74,31 @@
     const unsigned LOG_ROTATION_PERIOD = 3 * 60 * 60 * 1000; // 3 hours
     const size_t PACKER_FRAGMENTS_SIZE = 4096;
     constexpr size_t LINE_FRAGMENT_SIZE = 4096;
+
+    // Campfire (patch 0201): "a.b.c.d" or "a.b.c.d:port", nothing a resolver would look up.
+    bool IsIPv4Literal(const std::string& hostPort)
+    {
+        const std::string host = hostPort.substr(0, hostPort.find(':'));
+        int dots = 0, digits = 0, value = 0;
+        for (char c : host)
+        {
+            if (c == '.')
+            {
+                if (!digits || ++dots > 3)
+                    return false;
+                digits = value = 0;
+            }
+            else if (c >= '0' && c <= '9')
+            {
+                value = value * 10 + (c - '0');
+                if (++digits > 3 || value > 255)
+                    return false;
+            }
+            else
+                return false;
+        }
+        return dots == 3 && digits > 0;
+    }
 
